<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for <span class="c2">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_auraoflight.gif");'>Retribution Paladin</span></span> DPS in Cataclysm Classic in Phase 3. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="pre-raid-best-in-slot">
<span class="c2">Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear for Retribution Paladin DPS in Phase 3</span></h2>Paladins will focus primarily on melee damage-dealing statistics like Strength, Hit, Expertise, Mastery, Critical Strike, and Haste. You will need to reach the cap for hit chance and expertise to ensure that your attacks are not dodged or miss, causing a loss of potential Holy Power and damage.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Strength</b> - This is our primary stat, one that cannot be reforged, so we will take it wherever we possibly can most of the time. Strength converts into attack power and indirectly spell power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Hit Rating</b> - The Hit Rating cap is 8%, and you must reach this amount to ensure that your attacks do not miss, which can cause you to lose potential damage and Holy Power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Expertise Rating</b> - The Expertise cap is 6.5%, and you must reach this amount to ensure that your attacks are not dodged, which can cause you to lose potential damage and Holy Power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Mastery</b> - This stat adds additional holy damage to our primary abilities <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85256/templars-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_templarsverdict.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Templar's Verdict</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53385/divine-storm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_divinestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Storm</span></a>. Once Hit and Expertise caps are reached, this will be our most valuable secondary stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Critical Strike Chance</b> - Increases the chance to critically strike. A solid secondary stat, but not the best.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Haste</b> - Haste increases the rate at which we attack, but also with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=25956/sanctity-of-battle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_136.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctity of Battle</span></a> talented will reduce the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53385/divine-storm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_divinestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Storm</span></a>. That being said, it is our weakest secondary stat and we are unable to reach the point where it will bring <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a> cooldown to 3-seconds.</div></li></ol>This is the same order of stat importance when it comes to reforging, excluding Strength which cannot be reforged. Most players use an addon to calculate their reforges for them. We will be gemming <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52206/bold-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Bold Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Inferno Ruby</span></a> in almost every socket, occasionally using <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52213/etched-demonseye">
<img alt="Etched Demonseye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Demonseye</span></a> or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52240/skillful-ember-topaz">
<img alt="Skillful Ember Topaz" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skillful Ember Topaz</span></a> for Strength socket bonuses.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="justice-points">Justice Points for Retribution Paladin DPS in Phase 3</h3>All of the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items from Phase 1 and 2 are now found on the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> vendor. <br/>
<br/>None of the items here are pre-raid best in slot, and most of the decent items from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are easily replaced with better items - thus, spend these points filling in whatever gear you have not obtained from dungeons and reputation rewards. The most valuable <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> items are the Tier 11 Protection pieces (<i>see the paragraph below</i>), and the 359 item level epic quality items that were previously found on the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> vendor such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58185/band-of-bees">
<img alt="Band of Bees" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pearlring1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of Bees</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58190/floating-web">
<img alt="Floating Web" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_cataclysm_melee_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Floating Web</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>The Tier 11 Retribution items are not typically worth picking up unless you plan to upgrade them to 372 item level by raiding Phase 1 content and pair the Tier 11 2-set bonus with the Tier 12 2-set bonus; as you will otherwise instead use Tier 12 in these slots from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> and Normal Tier 11 helm/<wbr/>shoulders from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>. <br/>
<br/>The Tier 11 protection 4-set bonus offers a 50% increase to the duration of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86150/guardian-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_heroism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guardian of Ancient Kings</span></a>, which is often used by equipping the set bonus, and then using a macro to cast <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86150/guardian-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_heroism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guardian of Ancient Kings</span></a>, pre-pot, and swap to your Retribution set a few seconds before a raid boss is pulled, so you can benefit from the Tier 11 protection 4-set bonus without being forced to wear it for the fight. This pre-pull maneuver is explained in detail in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/paladin/retribution/dps-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve">Retribution Rotation &amp; Cooldowns Guide</a> and will be used for the rest of the expansion. It does significantly increase DPS, especially when you have the Tier 12 4-set Retribution bonus that extends the duration of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85696/zealotry">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_proclaimchampion_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zealotry</span></a>, so if you don't already have it, you will want to spend all of your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> getting the Tier 11 Protection items first, even before any Tier 11 Retribution items.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Retribution Paladin DPS in Phase 3</h3>Here is our recommended priority for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> purchases:<div class="pad"></div>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
