<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-retribution-paladin-dps">Trinkets for Retribution Paladin DPS</h4>We typically always want 1 active on-use trinket and 1 passive proc trinket. Active trinkets tend to be more powerful than passive trinkets, but cannot be used together at the same time, so the ideal scenario is to use active trinkets with our cooldowns and hope that our passive proc trinkets trigger during this window.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="active-trinkets">Active Trinkets</h5>The best active trinket is still <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68712/impatience-of-youth">
<img alt="Impatience of Youth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_idol_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Impatience of Youth</span></a> which is obtained from doing <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5095/tol-barad">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Tol Barad</span></a> daily quests and reaching Exalted with their reputation. If you still don't have this yet you should be doing those dailies every day as this trinket can last you until the Heroic version of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68972/apparatus-of-khazgoroth">
<img alt="Apparatus of Khaz'goroth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Apparatus of Khaz'goroth</span></a> which you will only get by raiding <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5723/firelands">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Firelands</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>The second best pre-raid active trinket is certainly <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68972/apparatus-of-khazgoroth">
<img alt="Apparatus of Khaz'goroth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Apparatus of Khaz'goroth</span></a>, which is a random trash drop from enemies in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5723/firelands">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Firelands</span></a>, and can eventually be upgraded into a stronger version: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69113/apparatus-of-khazgoroth">
<img alt="Apparatus of Khaz'goroth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Apparatus of Khaz'goroth</span></a>. This stronger Heroic version can only be acquired after you begin raiding <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5723/firelands">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Firelands</span></a> and begin looting the required <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71617/crystallized-firestone">
<img alt="Crystallized Firestone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_diablostone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crystallized Firestone</span></a> currency from the raid bosses, and this Heroic version is the best in slot active trinket for Phase 3 - this is our highest priority item to upgrade with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71617/crystallized-firestone">
<img alt="Crystallized Firestone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_diablostone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crystallized Firestone</span></a>. This trinket stacks a buff called <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=96923/titanic-power">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_titansgrip.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Titanic Power</span></a> and once you have 5 stacks you can use the trinket to unleash them to gain 508 mastery, critical strike rating, or haste rating <b>per stack</b> = 2,540 with full stacks. If you use this while <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70141/dwyers-caber">
<img alt="Dwyer's Caber" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_branch_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dwyer's Caber</span></a> is triggered, you will likely end up with critical strike, which is not as powerful as mastery - our best secondary stat, so these are tricky to use together.<div class="pad"></div>
