<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Retribution Paladin DPS</h3>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="two-handed-weapons-for-retribution-paladin-dps">Two-Handed Weapons for Retribution Paladin DPS</h4>Slower weapons tend to be stronger than faster weapons of the same item level, with 0.2 slower speed being worth about 9 extra item levels. This means that a 359 item level 3.8 speed weapon such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64377/zinrokh-destroyer-of-worlds">
<img alt="Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_zinrokh-sword.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds</span></a> would be equivalent to a theoretical 3.6 speed weapon at the 368 item level. Slower weapons do more damage because seals and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85256/templars-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_templarsverdict.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Templar's Verdict</span></a> are not normalized. <br/>
<br/>The best two-handed weapons are the PvP two-handers <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70183/ruthless-gladiators-bonegrinder">
<img alt="Ruthless Gladiator's Bonegrinder" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_pvp410_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ruthless Gladiator's Bonegrinder</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70224/ruthless-gladiators-bonegrinder">
<img alt="Ruthless Gladiator's Bonegrinder" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_pvp410_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ruthless Gladiator's Bonegrinder</span></a> that can be purchased with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=390/conquest-points">
<span>
<img alt="Conquest Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvpcurrency-conquest-horde.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conquest Points</span></span></a>. You can choose to use the sword, mace, or axe based on what you like the most and what racial benefits you have. The stronger 391 item level version will require the weaker 378 level version, 2200 arena rating and an additional 3400x <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=390/conquest-points">
<span>
<img alt="Conquest Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvpcurrency-conquest-horde.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conquest Points</span></span></a>, so this may be a tough farm for newer players gearing up for the first time and will require many weeks of grinding to acquire - but the weaker version is very easily acquired in the first week of the season. <br/>
<br/>The second best weapon pre-raid is either <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63679/reclaimed-ashkandi-greatsword-of-the-brotherhood">
<img alt="Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood</span></a> from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64377/zinrokh-destroyer-of-worlds">
<img alt="Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_zinrokh-sword.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds</span></a> from Archaeology, due to the slow 3.8 speed - both are essentially the same weapon, though <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63679/reclaimed-ashkandi-greatsword-of-the-brotherhood">
<img alt="Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood</span></a> has a negligible 2 extra secondary stats, making it infinitesimally better. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70164/masterwork-elementium-deathblade">
<img alt="Masterwork Elementium Deathblade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_73.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Masterwork Elementium Deathblade</span></a> is a new crafted weapon that is a bit on the fast side at 3.5 speed, but has a high 365 item level. <br/>It's marginally better than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59492/akirus-the-worm-breaker">
<img alt="Akirus the Worm-Breaker" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_grimbatolraid_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Akirus the Worm-Breaker</span></a>, but worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63679/reclaimed-ashkandi-greatsword-of-the-brotherhood">
<img alt="Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64377/zinrokh-destroyer-of-worlds">
<img alt="Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_zinrokh-sword.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59492/akirus-the-worm-breaker">
<img alt="Akirus the Worm-Breaker" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_grimbatolraid_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Akirus the Worm-Breaker</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63679/reclaimed-ashkandi-greatsword-of-the-brotherhood">
<img alt="Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood</span></a> can also be purchased with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, but save your stones and purchase the stronger <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63679/reclaimed-ashkandi-greatsword-of-the-brotherhood">
<img alt="Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood</span></a> instead. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74246/enchant-weapon-landslide">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Landslide</span></a>
